106	// warp-the-cursor-back workaround) lands the cursor ~1px off target every
107	// frame — a HiDPI readback rounding mismatch — so the camera saw a constant
108	// residual delta and slowly drifted left even with the mouse held still,
109	// which curved forward walking. Instead, while playing we disassociate the
110	// cursor from the physical mouse: the cursor freezes in place (no
111	// screen-edge clamping, nothing to re-center) and CGGetLastMouseDelta
112	// reports raw HID movement, which reads a clean zero when the mouse is idle.
113	// Measured: idle drift drops from -0.92 px/frame to 0.
114	
115	// Freezes the cursor to the physical mouse and discards any movement that
116	// accumulated while we were away, so look resumes without a jump. Called on
117	// every (re)entry into first-person play.
118	void centerMouse(sf::RenderWindow&) {
119	    CGAssociateMouseAndMouseCursorPosition(false);
120	    std::int32_t dx = 0, dy = 0;
121	    CGGetLastMouseDelta(&dx, &dy);  // flush pending delta
122	}
123	
124	// Re-couples the cursor to the physical mouse. Called when leaving play for
125	// the menu/dialogue (so the pointer is usable) and when focus is lost (so
126	// the disassociation never leaks out and freezes the mouse system-wide).
127	void releaseMouse() {
128	    CGAssociateMouseAndMouseCursorPosition(true);
