// The single authoritative "where the player is looking" vector, derived from
// yaw AND pitch. This is the fix for the gun-aim drift (the moonwalk class of
// bug): the camera and every weapon must derive their aim from THIS one
// function instead of each reconstructing a separate direction that drifts
// out of sync. Convention (matches RaylibRenderer::beginFrame's camera basis):
//   yaw 0  -> +Z,  yaw +90 -> +X,  pitch >0 -> +Y (looking up).
// Returns a normalized vector.
